.TH CHECKPKG 1 "September 2026" "Saphira Linux" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
checkpkg \- validate a package against the live repository
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B checkpkg
.I PACKAGE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B checkpkg
verifies that
.I PACKAGE
is really what the repository claims: present in
.IR Packages.adb ,
newest resolved by true version comparison (r10 > r9, which plain
string order gets wrong), every indexed artifact file present,
signatures valid, and on-disk metadata identity matching the index.
If a built-but-unpublished transaction exists for the package it
warns that
.BR installpkg (8)
will install the published version, and points at
.BR sign-apk-repo (8)
first.
.SH OPTIONS
This command takes no options beyond the package name.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $SAPHIRA_REPO_DIR/<generation>/$SAPHIRA_ARCH/Packages.adb
The trusted index everything is checked against.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Verified (a warning about unpublished staged work does not fail).
.TP
.B 1
Missing index, bad signature, missing artifact, identity mismatch,
or invalid package name.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS
checkpkg nginx
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR recipe (5),
.BR saphira (7),
.BR buildpkg (1),
.BR resolvepkg (1),
.BR installpkg (8),
.BR sign-apk-repo (8)
